Smart Beat's piano model (Record to tab, "High accuracy") is Transkun 2.0 converted to ONNX
(src-tauri/src/recording/transkun.rs and research/record-to-tab/piano/export_transkun.py port
its inference code). The converted files are not part of the installer: the app downloads them
once, with the user's consent, from the Smart Beat release "piano-model-1" and checks their sums.

The weights were trained on the MAESTRO dataset (Hawthorne et al., Google Magenta, CC BY-NC-SA 4.0)
with other piano data. The Transkun author publishes the weights under the MIT license. See
docs/licensing.md for what that means for Smart Beat.
